course: dictionary
lesson: 14611
title: Poplar: a tree or its wood?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can name a thing or the material that thing is made of. Context tells you which one. «Rows of poplars lined the road.» Here poplars are trees, because trees can be planted in rows. «The shelf was made of poplar.» Here poplar is the wood, because shelves are made out of wood.
explain: Look at the words around the word for clues. Rows, lined and road tell you we are talking about tall plants by the road. Made of tells you about material. Ask yourself: would a tree or wood fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Poplar is a noun. One tree is a poplar, and two or more are poplars, so you add s to make the plural.
fact: A poplar is a tall, fast-growing tree with soft wood.
fact: The leaves of a poplar often shake in the wind.
fact: Poplar also means the wood of this tree.
fact: Poplars are common in Europe and North America, often planted in rows along roads and rivers.
fact: Aspen and cottonwood are two kinds of poplar.
exercise: «Rows of poplars lined the road.» What are the poplars in this sentence? | A river boat | A kind of bird | *Tall trees | A type of road
exercise: «The shelf was made of poplar.» What does poplar mean here? | *The wood of a poplar tree | A soft kind of cloth | A dog that likes water | A tree growing in a field
exercise: «The poplar grew fast beside the river.» Find and copy one word that tells you how the tree grew. | the | beside | river | *fast
test: «The leaves of the poplar shook in the wind.» What do the leaves often do? | Fall off all at once | Turn into wood | *Shake | Lie flat and still
test: «Aspen and cottonwood are both kinds of which tree?» | Oak | *Poplar | Pine | Willow
exam: «Grandma's chair was carved from poplar.» What does poplar mean in this sentence? | A kind of chair | A river | A tall tree | *The wood of the tree
